<language>
	<!-- SeparatistRegiments -->
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Basilisk" value="Basilisk"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/BasiliskDescription" value="Long-range artillery tank unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/BasiliskFlavor" value="When the Guard go to war, they march to the thunderous report of batteries of Basilisks whose guns can flatten cities and end worlds. Instantly recognisable for the long, looming barrel of its earthshaker cannon, the Basilisk boasts a prodigious range."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Bullgryn" value="Bullgryns"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/BullgrynDescription" value="Heavy melee infantry unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/BullgrynFlavor" value="Bullgryns are clad in custom-made carapace armour and carry crude assault weaponry to capitalise on the abhumans' stature and resilience. These units provide their comrades with a wall of walking cover as they advance across the battlefield, soaking up vast volumes of enemy fire in the process. For the separatists, these giants are a rare and valuable find, since their prison worlds remain within the Imperium. Finding a loyal soldier and buying out his contract... takes considerable effort and resources."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Chimera" value="Chimera"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ChimeraDescription" value="Amphibious transport unit with manned weaponry and communication equipment."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ChimeraFlavor" value="The Chimera is the most prolific and popular armoured transport used by the Imperial Guard. It is rugged, versatile, and easy to produce in huge numbers. The separatists' modified version has weaker armor and a more powerful engine. It is less resistant to attacks, but its purpose is not to fight, but to provide mobility for the infantry."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Commissar" value="Commissar"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/CommissarDescription" value="Hero unit that provides bonuses to nearby allied units."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/CommissarFlavor" value="There is no place for aristocrats or titles among the separatists. A commissar is not a lord, but a soldier just like those he leads into battle. The difference is that he has the right to shoot a coward—and does so when necessary. But unlike his Imperial counterparts, he does not execute soldiers for retreating without cause. Discipline is not just fear. Discipline is when an order is carried out because they trust their commissar."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Deathstrike" value="Deathstrike"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/DeathstrikeDescription" value="Long-range artillery vehicle carrying a single, destructive missile."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/DeathstrikeFlavor" value="The sanctioned use of a Deathstrike launcher – designated ‘Ordnance Extremis’ – is often an excessive measure to combat the Imperium’s most heinous enemies. However, this massive rocket will now shine a new light on humanity’s enemies—whether human or xenos."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/DevilDog" value="Devil Dog"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/DevilDogDescription" value="Fast tank unit with a deadly armour-melting cannon."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/DevilDogFlavor" value="Acquiring its name from the high-pitched howl this weapon makes upon firing, the Devil Dog is capable of punching far above its weight in armoured combat, while remaining a fast and aggressive tank destroyer. The separatist modification added a troop compartment—now it can transport a squad of infantry. It’s hot and cramped inside, but at least the infantry isn’t exposed to fire while approaching."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/FieldOrdnanceBattery" value="Field Ordnance Batteries"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/FieldOrdnanceBatteryDescription" value="Large man-portable artillery unit able to shell out enemy positions at long range."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/FieldOrdnanceBatteryFlavor" value="On Gladius Prime, the separatists got their hands on Imperial “Bombast” artillery pieces. The Xenari re-calibrated the barrels and chambers, increasing the firing range, and adapted the fire control system to work with marker drones. The artillery crews are still just as unhurried, but now their shells fly farther."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Guardsman" value="Guardsmen"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/GuardsmanDescription" value="Light infantry unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/GuardsmanFlavor" value="They were tired of being cannon fodder for Imperial commissars. They had seen their comrades sent into hopeless attacks simply because “the regulations demand it.” They joined the separatists not out of any love for xenotechnology—they were simply promised that their deaths would have meaning. The new state isn’t much better than the Imperium in many ways, but at least here the officers think with their heads, not by the book. And that alone is reason enough to switch sides."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Headquarters" value="<string name='Buildings/SeparatistRegiments/Headquarters'/>"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/HeadquartersDescription" value="Headquarters unit that represents a city's defenses."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/HeadquartersFlavor" value="<string name='Buildings/SeparatistRegiments/HeadquartersFlavor'/>"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/HeavyWeaponsSquad" value="Heavy Weapons Squad"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/HeavyWeaponsSquadDescription" value="Infantry unit equipped to deal with heavily armoured targets."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/HeavyWeaponsSquadFlavor" value="Infantry heavy weapons are typically crewed by a team of two men; one fires the weapon while the other supplies the ammunition, and between them they can relocate their weapon if needs be."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Hydra" value="Hydra"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/HydraDescription" value="Fast tank unit that excels against airborne targets."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/HydraFlavor" value="Whether faced by lightning-fast xenos fighters or daemonic, leather-winged monstrosities, the Hydra Flak Tank is ideally equipped to blow aerial foes out of the sky. The Hydra's predictive logic-spirit singles out and locks onto its targets with the tenacity of a predatory beast."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ImperialStrongpoint" value="Imperial Bastion"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ImperialStrongpointDescription" value="Fortification with heavy bolters that can shelter infantry."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ImperialStrongpointFlavor" value="An Imperial Bastion is an imposing edifice built from foot-thick ferrocrete. It is relatively easy to build, and the separatists are already planning to cover their newly acquired territories with a network of such fortifications. The structure is capable of withstanding orbital strikes and artillery fire, although there are weapons capable of destroying it with a single hit. The Xenarites are still exploring ways to upgrade this structure, but for now, the bastions are being used as they were captured. It is no surprise that these fortresses will also become the cornerstone of the new state’s defense."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/LemanRussBattleTank" value="Leman Russ Battle Tank"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/LemanRussBattleTankDescription" value="Heavily armoured main battle tank unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/LemanRussBattleTankFlavor" value="The Leman Russ battle tank is an ironclad declaration of might made manifest. They are the mainstay of the Imperial Guard's armoured forces, lumbering slabs of armour and intolerance whose inexorable advance has ground a billion foes of New Humanity to bloody ruin."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/MarauderBomber" value="Marauder Bomber"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/MarauderBomberDescription" value="Super-heavy bomber unit that obliterates ground targets."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/MarauderBomberFlavor" value="Sturdily built and boasting a colossal payload for its size, the Marauder is the archetypal heavy bomber. Powerful engines and capacious fuel tanks give the Marauder a substantial operational reach and, furthermore, allow bomber squadrons to operate effectively in times of sporadic resupply."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/PrimarisPsyker" value="Primaris Psyker"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/PrimarisPsykerDescription" value="Hero unit without destructive psychic powers."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/PrimarisPsykerFlavor" value="Loathed and feared as witches by their superstitious comrades, Primaris Psykers are nonetheless valuable assets to any commander. Though it hardly lessens the constant suspicion they are held in by the Officio Prefectus, each of these psykers possess abilities and control far beyond those of lesser Scholastica Psykana initiates."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Ratling" value="Ratlings"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/RatlingDescription" value="Sniper infantry unit that can move after shooting."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/RatlingFlavor" value="Though less resilient than their human comrades, Ratlings are naturally excellent shots. It is said that Ratling marksmen can take the head off an enemy from over a kilometre away. Coupled with their knack for staying out of harm’s way, this makes Ratlings formidable snipers who can take a surprising toll upon superior enemy forces."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/RogalDornBattleTank" value="Rogal Dorn Battle Tank"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/RogalDornBattleTankDescription" value="Heavily armoured battle tank fitted with powerful weapons."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/RogalDornBattleTankFlavor" value="The Rogal Dorn Battle Tank is a lumbering behemoth, equally suited to anchoring a battle line, or grinding forward in support of an assault. Bristling with thunderous guns, these hulking armoured fighting vehicles pound breaches in enemy’s defences with enormous shells, and tear apart infantry with raucous storms of fire."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ScoutSentinel" value="Scout Sentinels"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ScoutSentinelDescription" value="Light armoured walker unit specialized in reconnaissance."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ScoutSentinelFlavor" value="The Sentinel is a fast-moving combat walker employed to scout dense terrain and provide close infantry fire support. With surprising speed and locomotive dexterity, Sentinels can traverse terrain that would confound other armoured vehicles. The lighter-armoured Scout Sentinels, in particular, are used to range ahead of the main battle line, setting up brutal ambushes or launching pin-point raids."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/SeparatistBulwark" value="Bulwark Fiery Sunset"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/SeparatistBulwarkDescription" value="A powerful defensive structure equipped with long-range artillery and a scaled-down version of the void shield."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/SeparatistBulwarkFlavor" value="The pinnacle of the Separatists’ engineering. This monolith, constructed from Armaplas and ferrocrete, combines the firepower of a Vasilisk battery, bolter turrets, and a lightweight hollow shield capable of deflecting even the most powerful strikes. This is not merely a bastion—it is a statement. The New Humanity has arrived, and it will not retreat from here."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TankCommander" value="Tank Commander"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TankCommanderDescription" value="Tank hero unit with formidable strength that also boosts nearby allied tank units."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TankCommanderFlavor" value="A Tank Commander rides to battle in the cupola of a mighty Leman Russ battle tank. These grizzled men are virtually one with their machine, possessing an implicit knowledge of armoured warfare in all its forms. The average Tank Commander is a steely eyed ace, heading up a crew of the very best their regiment has to offer."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TechpriestEnginseer" value="Tech-Priest Enginseers"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TechpriestEnginseerDescription" value="Infantry unit that supports vehicles, clears tiles and founds new cities."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TechpriestEnginseerFlavor" value="The Xenarites are a radical Mechanicus sect that studies xenos technologies. In the Imperium, they are considered heretics, but the Separatists have granted them sanctuary. Without these techno-priests, the Separatists’ heavy armor would quickly turn into a pile of scrap metal. They still whisper prayers to the machine spirits—but now they also rewire captured schematics."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TempestusScion" value="Tempestus Scions"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TempestusScionDescription" value="Elite shock infantry unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/TempestusScionFlavor" value="Regular separatist forces often look upon the young recruits with envy—the latter have better equipment and training. But the only thing keeping them from open hostility is the realization that what matters here is the ability to fight, not titles. Trained in covert operations and rapid-strike tactics, they go into battle confident that every action they take is for the good of the new state."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Thunderbolt" value="Thunderbolt"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ThunderboltDescription" value="Fast and heavy fighter unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ThunderboltFlavor" value="A heavy fighter that combines devastating strike potential with graceful speed and manoeuvrability, the Thunderbolt forms the bulk of the Imperial Navy's intra-atmosphere fighter aircraft. The Thunderbolt is a true workhorse, with a rugged and reliable design both venerated by its crews and respected by its enemies."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/Valkyrie" value="Valkyrie"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ValkyrieDescription" value="Versatile airborne transport unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/ValkyrieFlavor" value="The Valkyrie Assault Carrier is a well-armed, twin-engine attack craft. The durable armour and versatile payload of the Valkyrie chassis combine with the aircraft's powerful engines and stable handling to make it a popular choice for a broad spectrum of battlefield roles."/>
	
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/GunDrone" value="MV1 Drones"/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/GunDroneDescription" value="Basic combat drone unit."/>
	<entry name="SeparatistRegiments/GunDroneFlavor" value="Having witnessed the effectiveness of Tau drones in combat, the separatists decided that this technology was worth replicating. They reverse-engineered it using captured combat drones, creating the MV1—a model with less firepower but equipped with target acquisition capabilities as well. Soldiers don’t like it—it buzzes, smokes, and draws fire—but when the enemy appears, it’s the MV1 that fires first."/>
	
</language>
